<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Application</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  body {
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  h1, h2, h3 {
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  td {
    padding: 5px 0;
  }
  .header-table td {
    padding: 10px 0;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: right; font-size: 10pt;">1</div>
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 50px;">
    <img src="placeholder_logo.png" alt="University Logo" style="height: 60px; width: auto;">
    <h1 style="margin-top: 10px;">TENNESSEE STATE UNIVERSITY</h1>
    <h2>SCHOOL OF NURSING AASN APPLICATION</h2>
  </div>
  <p style="margin-top: 30px;">The Nursing Programs at <span data-field="university_name">{{ university_name }}</span> are limited enrollment programs based on faculty and clinical resources. Admission to the Associate of Applied Science in Nursing (AASN) Program is competitive. Composition of each class reflects the diversity of the applicant pool. Information regarding the admission of applicants is available from the School of Nursing and online at <span data-field="website_url">{{ website_url }}</span>. An applicant does not have to be admitted to TSU prior to submission of an application; however the applicant must be fully admitted to TSU in order to be offered admission to the Associate of Applied Science in Nursing Program.</p>

  <table style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 30%;">Name:</td>
      <td style="width: 30%;"><span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span></td>
      <td style="width: 40%;"></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Mailing Address:</td>
      <td><span data-field="mailing_address">{{ mailing_address }}</span></td>
      <td></td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <table style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 25%;">First</td>
      <td style="width: 25%;">Middle</td>
      <td style="width: 25%;">Last</td>
      <td style="width: 25%;">Maiden</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <table style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 30%;">City</td>
      <td style="width: 30%;">State</td>
      <td style="width: 20%;">Zip Code</td>
      <td style="width: 20%;">Home Phone</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <table style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 30%;">TSU (T-Number) or last four digits of social security number</td>
      <td style="width: 70%;"><span data-field="ssn_or_tsu_id">{{ ssn_or_tsu_id }}</span></td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <table style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <tr>
      <td>E-mail address</td>
      <td><span data-field="email_address">{{ email_address }}</span></td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">List all previous institutions attended: (Attach additional sheet(s) if needed):</h3>
  <table style="margin-top: 15px;">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Name of Institution</th>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Dates attended</th>
        <th style="width: 40%;">Degree earned</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for item in previous_institutions %}
      <tr>
        <td><span data-field="previous_institutions[{{ loop.index0 }}].institution_name">{{ previous_institutions[loop.index0].institution_name }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="previous_institutions[{{ loop.index0 }}].dates_attended">{{ previous_institutions[loop.index0].dates_attended }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="previous_institutions[{{ loop.index0 }}].degree_earned">{{ previous_institutions[loop.index0].degree_earned }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Associate of Applied Science in Nursing (AASN) Degree (2 year)</h3>
  <p>
    <span data-field="requirement_statement">{{ requirement_statement }}</span>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><span data-field="requirement_1">{{ requirement_1 }}</span></li>
    <li><span data-field="requirement_2">{{ requirement_2 }}</span></li>
    <li><span data-field="requirement_3">{{ requirement_3 }}</span></li>
    <li><span data-field="requirement_4">{{ requirement_4 }}</span></li>
    <li><span data-field="requirement_5">{{ requirement_5 }}</span></li>
    <li><span data-field="requirement_6">{{ requirement_6 }}</span></li>
    <li><span data-field="requirement_7">{{ requirement_7 }}</span></li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">In keeping with the required affirmative action and institution reporting at Tennessee State University, <span data-field="affirmative_action_statement">{{ affirmative_action_statement }}</span></p>

  <table style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 20%;">Ethnic Background</td>
      <td style="width: 10%;">Gender</td>
      <td style="width: 10%;">Age</td>
      <td style="width: 10%;">DOB</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Martial Status:</td>
      <td><input type="radio" name="marital_status" value="single"> Single</td>
      <td><input type="radio" name="marital_status" value="married"> Married</td>
      <td><input type="radio" name="marital_status" value="divorced"> Divorced</td>
      <td><input type="radio" name="marital_status" value="separated"> Separated</td>
      <td><input type="radio" name="marital_status" value="widowed"> Widowed</td>
      <td><input type="radio" name="marital_status" value="other"> Other</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Head of Household</td>
      <td><input type="text" style="width: 30%;" data-field="head_of_household" value="{{ head_of_household }}"></td>
      <td>Number of dependents</td>
      <td><input type="text" style="width: 30%;" data-field="number_of_dependents" value="{{ number_of_dependents }}"></td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <p style="margin-top: 30px;">The School of Nursing seeks to provide a reasonably safe environment for its nursing students and their clients. A student may be required, during the course of the program, to demonstrate their physical and/or emotional fitness to meet the essential requirements of our program. Such requirements may include, but are not limited to, freedom from communicable disease, the ability to perform certain physical tasks, and suitable emotional fitness. For a complete list of requirements, please refer to the last page of this application.</p>

  <p style="margin-top: 20px;">Any appraisal measures used to determine such physical and/or emotional fitness will be in compliance with Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and the American with Disabilities Act of 1990, so as not to discriminate against any individual on the basis of handicap.</p>

  <p style="margin-top: 30px;">(If accepted into the program):</p>
  <p>
    <span data-field="background_check_statement">{{ background_check_statement }}</span>
  </p>

  <p style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <span data-field="certification_statement">{{ certification_statement }}</span>
  </p>

  <p style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <span data-field="responsibility_statement">{{ responsibility_statement }}</span>
  </p>

  <table style="margin-top: 50px;">
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 50%;">PRINT NAME</td>
      <td style="width: 50%; text-align: center;">SIGNATURE</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
  <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: 50px;">AASN Application Revised 07/24/2019</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">PLEASE SUBMIT YOUR APPLICATION MATERIAL TO THE SCHOOL OF NURSING WITH ALL THE REQUIRED INFORMATION BY MARCH 16, 2020 FOR FALL ADMISSION</h2>

  <p style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">Applicants must submit the complete packet of materials. Incomplete packets will not be considered for admission to the program. Submit your completed application materials to:</p>

  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    Tennessee State University<br>
    School of Nursing<br>
    AASN Program (Admissions)<br>
    Humphries Hall, Suite 217<br>
    Nashville, Tennessee 37209-1561<br>
    (615) 963-5265 (phone); (615) 963-5264 (fax)<br>
    Email: <span data-field="application_email">{{ application_email }}</span>
  </div>

  <p style="margin-top: 30px;">Publication Number: <span data-field="publication_number">{{ publication_number }}</span> Tennessee State University is an AA/EEO employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability or age in its program and activities. The following person has been assigned to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: The Director of Equity, Diversity and Compliance, 3500 John A. Merritt Blvd. Nashville, TN 37209, (615) 963-7435.</p>

  <p style="margin-top: 20px;">Tennessee State University is committed to the education of a non-racially identifiable student body. Tennessee State University, in compliance with Title IV of the Civil Rights Act of 1964 and Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, does not discriminate on this basis of race, color, national origin, or sex in any of its policies or procedures. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, persons needing assistance with these materials may contact the School of Nursing.</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <table style="width: 100%; margin-top: 30px;">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 25%;">ISSUE</th>
        <th style="width: 35%;">STANDARD</th>
        <th style="width: 40%;">EXAMPLES OF ACTIVITIES (NOT ALL INCLUSIVE)</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Critical Thinking Ability</td>
        <td>Critical thinking ability sufficient for clinical judgment.</td>
        <td>Analyze complex situations, identify key issues, formulate hypotheses, and develop evidence-based solutions. Synthesize knowledge and skills. Sequence information.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Interpersonal Skills</td>
        <td>Interpersonal skills sufficient to interact with individuals, families and groups from a variety of cultural, social, emotional, and intellectual backgrounds.</td>
        <td>Establish rapport with patients and families. Communicate effectively with diverse populations. Demonstrate empathy and active listening skills.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Communication Ability</td>
        <td>Communication abilities sufficient for interaction with others in verbal and written form in English.</td>
        <td>Explain health conditions, diagnose and treat illnesses, and provide patient education. Document patient care accurately. Communicate effectively with team members and colleagues.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Mobility</td>
        <td>Physical abilities sufficient to move from room to room and maneuver in small spaces.</td>
        <td>Walk, stand, bend, stoop, climb on stool or stairs, and move around a patient's room. Transfer patients safely. Perform basic physical tasks required for nursing duties.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Motor Skills</td>
        <td>Gross and fine motor skills sufficient to provide safe and effective nursing care.</td>
        <td>Manipulate small objects with hands. Manipulate small objects with fingers. Use a pen on a computer keyboard.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Hearing Ability</td>
        <td>Auditory ability sufficient to monitor and assess health needs.</td>
        <td>Hear normal and faint sounds. Hear faint body sounds. Hear speech in noisy environments. Hear alarms and calls.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Visual Skills</td>
        <td>Visual ability sufficient for observation and assessment necessary in nursing care.</td>
        <td>See objects at various distances. Observe subtle changes in patient appearance. Distinguish colors and color intensity. Read and interpret charts.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Tactile Ability</td>
        <td>Tactile ability sufficient for physical assessment.</td>
        <td>Feel vibrations to detect pulses. Detect temperature. Feel textures and shapes.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Emotional Stability</td>
        <td>Emotional stability sufficient to tolerate rapidly changing conditions and stressful environments.</td>
        <td>Maintain composure under pressure. Manage stress and anxiety. Respond appropriately to stressful situations. Demonstrate resilience and adaptability.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p style="margin-top: 50px; font-size: 9pt;">Source: Southern Council on Collegiate Education for Nursing (1993) and National Council of State Boards of Nursing, Inc.: Guidelines for Using Results of Functional Abilities Studies and other Resources (1990) and Armstrong Atlantic State University (2010).</p>
  <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: 50px;">AASN Application Revised 07/24/2019</p>
</div>
</body>
</html>